@startuml

salt
{
  <b>RETIRE A CONVENTION</b>  { Document | Reach | Reason | Retired }
  --
  {
    {
      <b>1. The document</b>  -  swap, party ACCOUS
      --
      {#
        Field | Value
        Key | AED-EIBOR-6M-SWAP
        Version | 2
        Terms | AED, annual, ACT/365, AED-EIBOR-6M
        Same terms in | 0 other documents
      }
      <i>Retiring closes the row with valid_to. The history stays readable.</i>
      [ Read the reach ]
    } | {
      <b>2. What reads it</b>
      --
      {#
        Reader | State
        Conventions file of ACCOUS | carries every swap document
        Convention sets | named by 1 set
        Report definitions | bound through that set: 2
        Trades | carry their terms inline: none
      }
      <b>A run takes this row because it is in the party's document.</b>
      <i>Nothing in the server checks references before a delete.</i>
      [ Back ] | [ Continue ]
    }
  }
  --
  {
    {
      <b>3. Say why</b>
      --
      Reason: ^system.obsolete^v
      Commentary: ^Replaced by AED-EIBOR-6M-SWAP-2.^
      --
      <b>Retiring removes the row from the next run of ACCOUS.</b>
      Runs that read it before keep the version they read.
      [ Back ] | [ Ask for approval ]
    } | {
      <b>4. Retired</b>
      --
      <b>AED-EIBOR-6M-SWAP is retired at version 3</b>
      by m.okafor at 2026-10-19 10:12
      --
      <b>What retiring did not do</b>
      It did not choose a replacement: no default marker exists.
      It did not change the set that names it: the set now names a closed row.
      [ See the history ] | [ Back to the kind ]
    }
  }
}

@enduml
